WEBVTT


00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:06.470
You don't have to work increases and
decreases at the edge of your knitting.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:11.270
In this example, we're going to increase
in the center of the knitting for a

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:14.060
bust dart in a sideways knit sweater.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.590
We'll be using a garter bar to
move a large number of stitches.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.600
Start by marking the needle
that will be used for reference.

00:00:30.765 --> 00:00:34.905
To keep from dropping stitches, hang
a three-prong tool on the needles

00:00:34.905 --> 00:00:36.735
to the left of the marked needle.

00:00:36.945 --> 00:00:42.225
Just let it hang, remove the group
of stitches on the garter bar.

00:00:54.959 --> 00:00:59.129
Move them one needle to the
right, leaving an emptied needle.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.940
Then rehang the stitches
from the garter bar.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:29.535
Pick up the butt of a stitch in the
row below to fill the empty needle.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.574
One stitch has been increased.

00:01:38.685 --> 00:01:40.635
Following your knitting instructions.

00:01:40.635 --> 00:01:44.445
Repeat the increase for as many
times as needed for your pattern.

00:01:47.055 --> 00:01:51.885
To work decreases in the middle of the
knitting, start by transferring the Mark

00:01:51.885 --> 00:02:00.165
stitch to the left, leaving an emptied
needle, hanging that three-prong tool

00:02:00.195 --> 00:02:02.535
will keep the stitches from popping off.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:11.039
Then remove the group of
stitches on the garter bar,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.830
shift them to the left,
filling in that emptied needle.

00:02:31.515 --> 00:02:34.815
Take the newly emptied needle
to out of work position.

00:02:34.845 --> 00:02:39.255
And you will have decreased a stitch
in the middle of the knitting.

00:02:40.845 --> 00:02:43.965
Following your knitting
instructions, repeat the decrease

00:02:43.965 --> 00:02:45.765
for as many times as needed.

